  "dialogues": {
    "elder_thalia_greeting": "Ah, a traveler! Welcome to Emberwatch. I am Elder Thalia, keeper of this village's lore. You arrive at a troubling time — the ward that has shielded our valley for centuries is fading fast. If it fails, the corruption beyond the hills will pour in, and Emberwatch will fall.",
    "elder_thalia_offer": "The Ward Wand can renew the ward — a relic of the Vesperine Order, carved from the heartwood of the first ward tree. With it in my hands I can mend the ward and save the valley. But the wand was lost years ago. Word has it a rogue named Rollo the Grasper took it and now keeps it at the Guttering Candle inn, east of the square. Will you bring it back to me? Emberwatch would be forever in your debt.",
    "elder_thalia_progress": "Have you found the Ward Wand yet? Rollo the Grasper holds it at the inn, east of the village square. He is a stubborn, slippery sort — he may need convincing, or a firmer hand than words.",
    "elder_thalia_decline": "I understand — the burden is heavy and the roads are rough. Should you change your mind, I will be here, and the ward will still be fading.",
    "elder_thalia_complete": "You found it! The Ward Wand — I can feel its warmth from here. With this, the ward will blaze bright once more. Emberwatch owes you a debt it can never repay.",
    "elder_thalia_ending_renewed": "You returned the Ward Wand! The ward blazes bright once more — I felt its pulse from the village center. Emberwatch owes you everything, brave soul. The Vesperine Order smiles upon you.",
    "rollo_greeting": "What do you want? I'm busy. If it's about that glowing stick — it's mine. Found it fair and square off a dead man's hands. Now scram.",
    "rollo_ask_wand": "The Ward Wand? Sure, I've got it. Pretty thing — hums when you hold it. But it's worth a fortune to the right buyer, and you're not that buyer. Go on, get lost.",
    "rollo_persuasion_success": "Hmph. You make a decent argument, adventurer. Emberwatch folk are good people, and if the ward dies we're all in the muck anyway. Fine — take the wand. Don't make me regret this.",
    "rollo_persuasion_failure": "Nice try. I've heard better sob stories from street rats. The wand stays with me. Come back when you have real coin — or real steel.",
    "rollo_intimidation_success": "W-wait! Easy now! Fine, fine — take it! It's not worth dying over a glowing stick. J-just don't hurt me!",
    "rollo_intimidation_failure": "Ha! You think a few harsh words scare me? I've stared down worse than you in alleys across the realm. Try again when you've grown a spine.",
    "rollo_fight_start": "Oh, you want it the hard way? Fine! Let's see how tough you really are!",
    "rollo_defeated": "Enough! Mercy! Take the wand — it's yours! Just... just let me keep my teeth.",
    "rollo_news": "Hear a lot, sitting here. The ward's failing — everyone knows it. That's why I'm holding onto the wand, see. When the price is right, I'll sell it back to the very folk who need it. Business.",
    "merchant_mara_greeting": "Welcome to Mara's Provisions! Fine steel, sturdy armor, potent potions — everything an adventurer needs to stay alive out there. What can I get for you today?",
    "merchant_mara_wand": "The Ward Wand? Oh yes — Rollo's prized trinket. He's been trying to sell it for months, but no buyer with a brain will touch it. The elder would pay dearly to have it back, though. Talk to Rollo at the Guttering Candle inn, east side of the village. And mind your coin purse around him.",
    "merchant_mara_news": "The whole valley's on edge, dear. The ward's fading, the elder's frantic, and that lout Rollo's been bragging at the inn that he holds the one thing that can fix it — the Ward Wand. If you're planning to deal with him, buy some potions first. You'll need them."
  },
